\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Per-cell histogram of the criterion fraction $\mathrm  {CF}$ across the $4{,}410$-cell sweep (columns: reward variant; rows: decorrelation $\rho \in \{0, 0.2\}$). The distribution --- a broad mode near $\mathrm  {CF}\approx 0.65$, a left tail (much heavier in variant~B), and a spike at $\mathrm  {CF}= 1$ --- characterises how the criterion fraction is spread across the parameter space. The $\rho = 0.2$ row exhibits the decorrelation amplification of the left tail quantified below.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cf-histogram}{{1}{8}{Per-cell histogram of the criterion fraction $\CF $ across the $4{,}410$-cell sweep (columns: reward variant; rows: decorrelation $\corr \in \{0, 0.2\}$). The distribution --- a broad mode near $\CF \approx 0.65$, a left tail (much heavier in variant~B), and a spike at $\CF = 1$ --- characterises how the criterion fraction is spread across the parameter space. The $\corr = 0.2$ row exhibits the decorrelation amplification of the left tail quantified below}{figure.1}{}}
